Standalone conformance & stress binaries for the native 5BSD squeue (Shared
Queue) engine and its Linux io_uring front-end.

The squeue engine has two front-ends over one shared kernel engine: the native
squeue_* syscalls and the Linux io_uring ABI.  There is one standalone binary
per interface, so both faces of the engine can be validated directly on an
installed system without the source tree or the kyua/ATF harness:

    squeue_check   native 5BSD front-end.  A normal FreeBSD binary.
    iouring_check  Linux io_uring front-end.  A freestanding Linux/amd64
                   static binary run under the Linuxulator (needs linux64).

Both emit TAP: "ok N - desc" / "not ok N - desc" lines and a trailing "1..N"
plan; exit status is 0 iff every check passed.  If the engine is absent each
prints "1..0 # SKIP" and exits 0.  Both require root and amd64.

BUILD
    make                 # squeue_check (native)
    make iouring_check   # Linux companion (needs clang + lld)
    make both            # both

    # or by hand, anywhere:
    cc -O2 -Wall -o squeue_check squeue_check.c -lpthread
    clang --target=x86_64-linux-gnu -fuse-ld=lld -nostdlib -static \
        -fno-stack-protector -fno-builtin -O2 -o iouring_check iouring_check.c

RUN
    ./squeue_check                 # native, TAP
    ./squeue_check -v              # verbose diagnostics
    ./squeue_check -q              # quick smoke (minimal iterations)
    ./squeue_check -i 10           # 10x the stress/soak iteration counts
    kldload linux64; ./iouring_check   # Linux front-end, TAP
    prove -e ./squeue_check :::     # summarize via prove(1)

COVERAGE
    squeue_check (native): setup/mmap, NOP, WRITE/READ, bad-fd errno,
        TIMEOUT, IOSQE_ASYNC round-trip, negative-offset guard, ring as a
        kqueue source, REGISTER_EVENTFD, CQSIZE/CLAMP, soft/hard IO_LINK,
        combinatorial op x flag matrix, ring-lifecycle wired-memory leak
        check, 8-thread concurrent async I/O, poll-wait + async
        (poll-path lost-wakeup regression), capsicum capmode confinement.
    iouring_check (Linux): setup/mmap, NOP, WRITE/READ, Linux bad-fd errno,
        TIMEOUT (-ETIME), IOSQE_ASYNC round-trip, CQSIZE/CLAMP, soft/hard
        IO_LINK, poll-wait + async -- the same conformance surface through
        the Linux ABI, confirming the shared engine behaves identically
        from both front-ends.

The exhaustive Linux battery lives in tests/sys/kern/linux_iouring.c (250+
subtests); iouring_check is the compact, packageable smoke/conformance
counterpart.  For per-event tracing of a live workload see the DTrace scripts
in the dtrace package: /usr/share/dtrace/squeue-flow, squeue-summary,
squeue-stall.
